from ./Escapes import Escapes

export anchor Comments:
    description:
        Emul comments follow the same rules as Piton comments. They are
        notes for the reader, and the compiler ignores them.

    lineOnly:
        Comments are line-only. There are no block comments.

    marker:
        A comment starts with `//` and runs to the end of the line.

    ownLine:
        A comment has to be on its own line, with nothing but indentation
        before the `//`. At the end of a line of code, `//` is just part of
        the value. This matters for values that contain `//` themselves, such
        as image URLs.

    placement:
        Comments may appear anywhere a line may: at the top level of a file,
        between the properties of a component, and between the entries of a
        composition. A comment does not end a component's indented block.

    escaping:
        To start a line with a literal `//` rather than a comment, escape it
        as described in @{Escapes}.

    formatting:
        The formatter always puts a space between the `//` and the comment
        text, and leaves the rest of the comment as it is, so commented-out
        code is kept intact.

    example:
        ```emul
        \\\
        // The buttons for the marketing site
        component HeroBanner:
            // The image URL keeps its // because this is not its own line
            backgroundImage: url(https://example.com/hero.png)
            backgroundSize: cover

        composition Home {
            // The banner is the only child of the root
            HeroBanner { "Welcome" }
        }
        \\\
        ```
